WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:07.760
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain a Japanese comedy drama film called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:15.920
“When I Get Home, My Wife Always Pretends to Be&nbsp;
Dead.” Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.440
Jun Kagami is a regular office worker living in&nbsp;
Tokyo with his wife Chie Kagami. Jun believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.320
that if a marriage lasts for more than three&nbsp;
years without much hardship, the couple is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.440
made for each other. His first marriage ended&nbsp;
after three years, so before marrying Chie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.640
the two had made an agreement to renew their&nbsp;
marriage contract after their third anniversary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.360
If they feel like they can no longer be together,&nbsp;
they will simply walk out of each other’s life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.800
Currently, the pair’s third marriage anniversary&nbsp;
is approaching and Jun is nervous about how their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.600
future will play out. While thinking about&nbsp;
such things, he returns home from work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.200
He rings the doorbell but no one answers. It is&nbsp;
quite unusual because Chie always welcomes him at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:07.840
the door. Jun uses the spare key to get inside and&nbsp;
is met with a horrifying sight. Chie is lying limp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.680
on the floor with blood dripping from her mouth.&nbsp;
He falls beside her and tries to wake her up but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.200
to no avail. In the moment of panic, Jun remembers&nbsp;
all the good times he has shared with his wife.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.560
On their wedding day, she had asked him to die&nbsp;
before her so she wouldn’t have to live without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.480
him. A few seconds later, Jun comes back to his&nbsp;
senses and composes himself. He tries calling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:36.080
for an ambulance when suddenly, Chie grabs his&nbsp;
legs, revealing that it was just a prank. 
&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.840
As Jun looks at her in shock, she asks him if he&nbsp;
is surprised and giggles. When he doesn’t reply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.320
she simply asks him to come to the kitchen for&nbsp;
dinner. After Jun has come out of his shocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:51.600
state, he jokes about Chie using ketchup as&nbsp;
fake blood. The couple laughs as Chie mocks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.960
Jun’s reaction to the prank. For the rest of&nbsp;
the dinner, their mood is happy and lightened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:02.080
The following morning, Chie asks for a kiss before&nbsp;
Jun leaves for work. He tells her they are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:08.080
newlyweds anymore so it is just cringe. Chie,&nbsp;
however, doesn’t share his views. She hugs him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.320
tightly claiming that they never know what will&nbsp;
happen during the day so this might be their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:18.240
last goodbye. On his way out, Jun drops off the&nbsp;
grange bag into the bins. A cleaning lady goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.960
through them and sees the bloodied clothes&nbsp;
from yesterday. She starts to believe Jun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.320
is doing something sketchy in his apartment.&nbsp;
In the office, Jun tells his co-worker Sano&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.360
about the prank Chie pulled on him yesterday. Sano&nbsp;
compliments Chie for putting effort to be funny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:45.200
and wishes his wife was less serious. Jun thinks&nbsp;
that Chie is testing to see if he still loves her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.080
so it would be easier to decide if she wants&nbsp;
to stay with him even after three years. 
&nbsp;

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.160
Later, in the evening, Chie is cooking&nbsp;
dinner when she gets a text from Jun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.560
saying that he is returning home.&nbsp;
She smiles mischievously at the text,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:04.800
ready for her next prank. Some minutes later, Jun&nbsp;
walks in and sees his wife lying on the floor with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:10.640
her head inside a realistic alligator’s mouth.&nbsp;
She is pretending to be eaten by the animal. Jun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.600
plays along and pulls her out of its mouth to&nbsp;
“save” her. She dramatically thanks her husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.800
for saving her life and says that they should eat&nbsp;
dinner now. Following that, Chie continues to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.320
dead every day, getting more creative with each&nbsp;
prank. One day, she pretends to be a maid who died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:32.240
after being caught in a conflict. Following that,&nbsp;
she is a trapped soldier shot by the enemies. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.200
the one that impresses Jun the most is when she&nbsp;
pretends to be shot by an arrow through her head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.240
He compliments the creativeness, although he is&nbsp;
getting more and more bothered by the pranks as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.680
time passes. Jun cannot decipher why she is doing&nbsp;
them, and with the third anniversary approaching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.480
it worries him even more. One day, he is&nbsp;
dumping the garbage again, which now mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.280
contains props that Chie uses to pretend to be&nbsp;
dead. The cleaning lady goes through the bag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:02.560
and finds a bloodied knife. She makes a scene&nbsp;
in front of everyone and calms down only when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:08.320
Jun explains to her that the blood is ketchup. 
He again expresses his uneasiness to his coworker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:16.880
Sano who suggests he send Chie to her parent’s&nbsp;
home for a few days. As they talk, Jun begins to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:22.560
tell him how he first met Chie and got to know&nbsp;
her. He was in Shizuoka for a business meeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.760
but he missed his bus back home. Chie saw him&nbsp;
running behind it and invited him to her father’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.960
restaurant. She was a pretty young girl but her&nbsp;
cheerful personality is what caught Jun’s eyes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.360
Her mother had passed away when she was&nbsp;
only five but she never let her sadness show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:42.800
in front of people. Before leaving, she had told&nbsp;
him her wish was to eat a dessert from Mont Saint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:48.480
Clair in Tokyo and he invited her to the city&nbsp;
sometime later. Sano is pleasantly surprised by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.320
the unique love story. That day, Jun returns home&nbsp;
to see Chie has turned herself into an old soldier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.840
from the medieval period who died in the war. She&nbsp;
has used several arrows because Jun had praised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.880
her the last time. He plays along and pretends&nbsp;
to be sad about her death. But he doesn’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:10.000
to pretend anymore when he sees the price tag&nbsp;
on the costume she is wearing. The next day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.720
he tells Sano that he is going to play along with&nbsp;
the pranks to see if she will stop doing them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:20.080
Hence, when he returns home and sees her being&nbsp;
abducted by fake aliens, he puts on the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:25.680
performance of his life and fights them.
However, it doesn’t stop Chie, instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:31.200
she prepares him an elaborate skit, asking him&nbsp;
to perform better. One time, she pretends to be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:37.120
dead vampire who has to be revived by pulling out&nbsp;
the dagger on her chest. Jun does as the skit says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:43.120
and gets bitten by her in the process. Following&nbsp;
that, she pretends to be Juliet who needs Romeo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:48.400
help to be revived from the dead. Similar to the&nbsp;
last time, Jun acts like he is mourning and brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:54.080
her back to life. At work, he cannot focus&nbsp;
anymore and is almost scared to return home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:58.400
Sano sympathizes with his work friend. To&nbsp;
make him avoid the pranks for just a day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:02.720
he invites the couple to dinner with his wife.&nbsp;
They all meet at a restaurant at the end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:08.880
day. Sano’s wife Yumiko also joins them. While&nbsp;
talking, Chie is asked why she decided to marry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.880
Jun. A flashback shows us that after meeting at&nbsp;
the restaurant, the pair met in Tokyo as well. Jun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:19.840
takes Chie to the cafe she always wanted to visit.&nbsp;
While walking through the streets of Tokyo, Chie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:25.520
runs after a street vendor that sells her favorite&nbsp;
wafer cake. Jun bolts behind her and finally gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.720
to the vendor. Since he has only one cake left,&nbsp;
they share it. Chie gives him the bigger piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:35.520
but Jun asks her to have the bigger one.&nbsp;
This was when she fell in love with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:40.160
Back in the present, while returning home, Jan&nbsp;
falls in love with his wife again. They look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:45.440
the moon and appreciate its beauty together.
One day, on his way home, Jun notices an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:50.240
advertisement for a vacancy at a local laundry&nbsp;
place. He thinks if Chie starts working,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:57.360
she will have less time for the pranks so&nbsp;
he brings the paper home. She welcomes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.720
dressed as an Egyptian princess inside a coffin.&nbsp;
After the dramatic encounter, they simply walk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:07.600
to the kitchen for dinner. Jun tells her&nbsp;
about the vacancy and urges her to apply.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:12.720
Chie is skeptical at first but she agrees to&nbsp;
do it anyway. Starting the next day, she works&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.920
at the laundry shop owned by an old man. Yet,&nbsp;
it doesn’t stop her from executing the pranks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.800
She pretends to be killed by a bank robber that&nbsp;
evening. Having had enough, Jun tells her that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:28.960
he is tired of seeing her play dead. The next day,&nbsp;
Chie goes on a date with Sano’s wife Yumiko, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:34.400
finds out she has been trying to get pregnant for&nbsp;
six years but hasn’t been successful. The couple’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:40.000
relationship is rocky because of this but Chie’s&nbsp;
kind words make Yumiko feel better. Jun brings his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.960
wife flowers and her favorite cake but when he&nbsp;
enters the apartment, he sees her pretending to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.560
be a ghost rising from her grave. Since he asked&nbsp;
her to not play dead, she pretended to be a ghost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:56.560
who is already dead. She hugs him for the cake&nbsp;
and cooks him something good for dinner. On the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:01.680
weekend, she pretends to be a robot but Jun&nbsp;
forcefully makes her take the mask off. 
&nbsp;

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:06.320
Following that, he notices a letter from his&nbsp;
former wife asking him to meet her someday. 
&nbsp;

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:11.680
The pair invites Sano and his wife to dinner one&nbsp;
day. Yumiko notices the alligator toy in the room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:16.880
and is fascinated by it. It turns out that she&nbsp;
is very much into alligators which surprises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:22.320
even her husband. Everything goes well until&nbsp;
Sano mentions that men need time off from their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:27.440
wives. This upsets Yumiko and she gets into an&nbsp;
argument with Sano. To make her feel better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:32.880
Chie offers her the alligator if she wins a match&nbsp;
of arm wrestling against her. Yumiko wins because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:38.720
she used to train at karate. She happily takes the&nbsp;
alligator home. Sano feels bad because he didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:44.240
know his wife’s interests even after being married&nbsp;
for six years. The following day, Jun comes home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:50.240
to see Chie has turned herself into a person from&nbsp;
2050. For the first few minutes, he plays along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:55.360
and asks her questions about the future. But&nbsp;
then, he inquires what he has to do for her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.320
to stop pulling these pranks. Chie goes silent&nbsp;
and starts to calculate the average number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:06.080
days they will spend together in the future. Even&nbsp;
when he persists, she doesn’t answer his question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:12.240
Some days later, Yumiko tells Chie that she and&nbsp;
Sano have decided to separate. She thanks Chie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:17.360
for making her feel appreciated. Because of her,&nbsp;
the couple was able to talk about their feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.720
to each other. Somewhere else, Jun and Sano go&nbsp;
to a restaurant to talk about the matter. 
&nbsp;

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.120
Sano claims that the divorce is a good decision&nbsp;
for both of them because Yumiko deserves a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.000
attentive partner. Jun also reveals that&nbsp;
his ex-wife once disappeared for two weeks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.800
and came back saying she wanted a divorce.&nbsp;
By the end of the night, he is very drunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.520
so Chie picks him up. The following day,&nbsp;
they get the news about Chie’s father being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:46.560
in the hospital because of a heart attack. They&nbsp;
quickly rush to her hometown and meet her father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:52.080
who has thankfully been saved. Chie meets him but&nbsp;
cannot control her tears afterward. When she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.800
not in the room, her father tells Jun that she&nbsp;
hasn’t cried since her mother’s death. He also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:02.400
mentions that one night after her mother died,&nbsp;
Chie saw him crying while looking at her picture.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.640
Starting the next day, she began to hide&nbsp;
around the house when he returned from work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:10.720
At first, her father thought it was&nbsp;
troublesome and weird but as time went on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:16.480
the simple activity of her hiding made him get&nbsp;
over his wife’s death because he was occupied. Jun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:21.840
realizes that he also has been more involved in&nbsp;
their relationship since she started to play dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:27.120
He registers that her pranks are not a result of&nbsp;
her being unsatisfied but she just wanted to feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:33.280
closer to him and keep him entertained. Later,&nbsp;
the two go to the park where Jun proposed to her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.120
They spend the rest of their day talking&nbsp;
to each other about different things. 
&nbsp;

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:43.120
The pair returns to Tokyo after a few days. Chie&nbsp;
comes back home after work to see Jun lying on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:48.720
floor with blood spewing from his mouth. She&nbsp;
freaks out and tries to wake him up but soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:54.960
realizes he is also pulling a prank. The movie&nbsp;
ends as Jun suggests they have dinner but Chie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:59.360
is too mad at him for scaring her like that. 
